        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Yuen Woo-ping, Basil Dean, Yuen Biao, Bryan Leung, Kwan Tak-hing, Gracie Fields, Alfred Drayton, Douglas Wakefield\n- Films: Dreadnaught, Look Up and Laugh\n- Roles: martial arts choreographer, film director, actor, writer, film producer, theatrical producer\n- Topics: Hong Kong action cinema, British comedy films, martial arts films\n\nFacts:\n- Basil Dean was born on 27 September 1888 and died on 22 April 1978.\n- Basil Dean was an English actor, writer, film producer, film director, theatrical producer, and theatrical director.\n- Look Up and Laugh is a 1935 British comedy film directed by Basil Dean and starring Gracie Fields, Alfred Drayton, and Douglas Wakefield.\n- Yuen Woo-ping was born in 1945.\n- Yuen Woo-ping is a Chinese martial arts choreographer and film director known as one of the most successful and influential figures in Hong Kong action cinema.\n- Dreadnaught is a 1981 Hong Kong martial arts film directed by Yuen Woo-ping and starring Yuen Biao, Bryan Leung, and Kwan Tak-hing.",
